# Keep host artifacts out of the clean-room build context.
#
# The Docker image is grove's portability proof: it must build the binary from
# source using ONLY the declared deps. If host-built artifacts leak in, the
# proof is void. In particular bin/grove is built for the host architecture
# (e.g. macOS arm64) and would fail to exec inside the Linux image — the fixture
# generator picks it up via its default -grove path and dies with
# "exec format error". Exclude it, and VCS/editor noise while we're here.
bin/
.git/
.github/
*.log
.DS_Store
